==== Sentence for the text (numbers as obtained) ====
With a point design prior, the frequentist Wilson-interval event gives N = 578, and Bayesian credible
intervals with a vague analysis prior give N = 576 (Jeffreys) and 579 (uniform), so the interval type alone
moves N by at most 2. Replacing the point design by the Beta design priors of the example, with the same
vague analysis priors, changes N to 824 (Jeffreys) and 831 (uniform), a change of +248 and +252 relative to
the point-design values (effect of design uncertainty). Replacing the vague analysis priors by the
informative priors of the example, with the point design, changes N from 576-579 to 466 (effect of the
informative analysis prior, -110 to -113). The worked example combines both changes (Beta design, informative
analysis): N = 672, that is +94 relative to the frequentist reference 578; the design uncertainty and the
informative analysis prior act in opposite directions. Along the path point design with Jeffreys analysis,
Beta design with Jeffreys analysis, Beta design with informative analysis: 576, 824, 672 (+248, then -152).

(The sentence is generated from the table; check the sign of each effect before reusing the wording: design effect on vague analysis = +248 / +252, analysis effect under point design = -110 / -113, analysis effect under Beta design = -152 / -159.)

